Z||000000||Deicide||11-15-2000||11:12 AM||||I might be buying an '86 Fiero 4 cylinder but it needs a new transmission because the current one is locked up.  I have a few questions about this.<P>Would the 5 speed Getrag work with this engine?  I plan to put in a larger engine in the future so getting the Getrag now would save me some money.<P>If the Getrag wouldn't work, does anyone know if GM or Izuzu had other cars that used the 5 speed FWD transmission?  Hopefully I'd be able to find one from a junkyard because I got a quote from a shop that said it would cost $1800 to get a reconditioned transmission and put it in.  Of course I can get it put in free by a class at the college I attend, so I'm wondering how much of that was the transmission cost.<P>Any help would be greatly appreciated.  I need to decide whether I want this car before Friday.<P><P>------------------<BR>--Deicide||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||11-15-2000||12:03 PM||||You may be able to pick up a used transmission from Ed Parks in Alabama or Bob Steiger in Illinois or another used Fiero parts resource just like the one in your current car.  I would expect that they would sell a used working transmission at a reasonable price, a working transmission is something a junkyard may not guarentee. Easy install a replacement for a collage class. Since you are planning to upgrade the car in the future, may save some modification hassles, if the Getrag needs some to connect to the 4 cylinder. Getrag transmissions are getting pricy for a Fiero.  When you upgrade get the engine and transmission and put the whole thing together off line.  My $0.02.||||reg||10
